  "solution": "**Given:**\n\na = 120\n\nb = 174\n\nc = 126\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\ns = (a + b + c) ÷ 2\n\nArea = √[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)]\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ s = (120 + 174 + 126) ÷ 2\n\n⇒ = 420 ÷ 2\n\n⇒ = 210\n\n⇒ s - a = 210 - 120 = 90\n\n⇒ s - b = 210 - 174 = 36\n\n⇒ s - c = 210 - 126 = 84\n\n⇒ Area = √(210 × 90 × 36 × 84)\n\n⇒ = √[(21 × 10) × (9 × 10) × 36 × (12 × 7)]\n\n⇒ = √(21 × 9 × 36 × 12 × 7 × 100)\n\n⇒ = √(21 × 9 × 36 × 12 × 7) × 10\n\n⇒ = √( (21 × 7) × (9 × 36 × 12) ) × 10\n\n⇒ = √(147 × 3888) × 10\n\n⇒ = √(147 × 3888) × 10\n\n⇒ = √( (49 × 3) × (1296 × 3) ) × 10\n\n⇒ = √(49 × 1296 × 9) × 10\n\n⇒ = √49 × √1296 × √9 × 10\n\n⇒ = 7 × 36 × 3 × 10\n\n⇒ = 7560\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 7560.**",
